tel 1.0 propensive.dev/bolt

# Bolt codes of Consequent Style: `subdivision 2` / `error 2` / `variant 1` is ↯/c.2.2.1, the
# first failure of the second rule of the second principle, Anchoring. Each principle is a
# subdivision, numbered in the order the standard sets them out; each rule, an error, numbered in
# the order of Part II; each distinct failure of a rule, a variant. The rules were identified
# before as `A2.1` (and before that in Soundness's `SN-` scheme), which `doc/rules/README.md` in
# propensive/flare maps onto these codes. A checker reports a violation under a code of its own
# carrying the rule's: flare's is `↯/f.21.1/c.2.2.1`.

project c consequent
  description  Consequent Style, the layout standard for Scala which flare checks

  subdivision 1 frame
    description  The Frame: the fixed shape every file sits in
    error 1 LicenceFrame
      description  Licence-header block comment
      source doc/rules/c.1.1.md
    error 2 PackageDeclaration
      description  `package` declaration on line `header + 1`
      source doc/rules/c.1.2.md
    error 3 PackageBlank
      description  Blank line after `package`
      source doc/rules/c.1.3.md
    error 4 LineLength
      description  Line length
      source doc/rules/c.1.4.md
    error 5 RawTabs
      description  Tab characters
      source doc/rules/c.1.5.md
    error 6 IndentWidth
      description  Indent width must be even
      source doc/rules/c.1.6.md
    error 7 TrailingWhitespace
      description  Trailing whitespace
      source doc/rules/c.1.7.md
    error 8 CommentShape
      description  Block-comment usage
      source doc/rules/c.1.8.md
      variant 1
        description  No /** … */ doc comments
      variant 2
        description  No /* … */ block comments outside the licence

  subdivision 2 anchoring
    description  Anchoring: where a continuation line begins
    error 1 ContinuationIndent
      description  Continuation indent
      source doc/rules/c.2.1.md
    error 2 SequenceLayout
      description  Keyword-sequence layout
      source doc/rules/c.2.2.md
      variant 1
        description  keyword <elem> must start on the same line as <anchor> (line <anchorLine>) or on a new line in column <anchorCol> (found line <elem>, column <elem>)
      variant 2
        description  body after <elem> must be indented onto a new line because an earlier body in this sequence is
    error 3 DefinitionAnchors
      description  Type-annotation anchor
      source doc/rules/c.2.3.md
    error 4 HeavyBracketAnchor
      description  Anchor of a heavy argument block
      source doc/rules/c.2.4.md
    error 5 BodyScopeIndent
      description  Indented scope body
      source doc/rules/c.2.5.md
    error 6 SignatureEqLast
      description  Signature `=` placement
      source doc/rules/c.2.6.md
    error 7 GivenArrowAlign
      description  `given` continuation alignment
      source doc/rules/c.2.7.md
    error 8 InterpolationLayout
      description  Multi-line interpolated-string layout
      source doc/rules/c.2.8.md
      variant 1
        description  the content of a multi-line <info><q> string must begin on the line after the opening quotes
      variant 2
        description  the content of a multi-line <info><q> string must be indented to column <expected>
      variant 3
        description  a line of a multi-line <info><q> string must not be indented less than the first content line (column <expected>)
      variant 4
        description  the closing <q> of a multi-line <info><q> string must be alone on its line, aligned with the opening quotes (column <col>)
    error 9 QuoteSpliceLayout
      description  Quote and splice layout
      source doc/rules/c.2.9.md
      variant 1
        description  closing } of a multi-line quote/splice at column <cols> does not align with its opening { at column <opener>
      variant 2
        description  <arr> and { of a multi-line quote/splice must be separated by exactly one space
      variant 3
        description  the <arr> { opener of a multi-line quote/splice must be alone on its line (only enclosing ( / { permitted)
      variant 4
        description  body of a multi-line quote/splice must be indented to column <top> (found <leadingCols>)
      variant 5
        description  closing } of a multi-line quote/splice must be alone on its line (only trailing ) / } permitted)
      variant 6
        description  no space is permitted directly after <prefix><text> in an inline quote/splice

  subdivision 3 density
    description  Density: how much to fit on one line
    error 1 UnnecessaryBreak
      description  Unnecessary line break
      source doc/rules/c.3.1.md
    error 2 LambdaLayout
      description  Lambda bracketing
      source doc/rules/c.3.2.md
      variant 1
        description  named-parameter lambda must be wrapped in {…}, not (…) (or use f: x => … since the lambda is last on the line)
      variant 2
        description  lambda is the last thing on its line; prefer f: x => … over f { x => … }
      variant 3
        description  multi-line lambda must use a colon-arg f: x => … form, not <s>
      variant 4
        description  anonymous (_-)lambda must be wrapped in (…), not <s>

  subdivision 4 continuation-marking
    description  Continuation Marking: showing that a line is unfinished
    error 1 ChainContinuation
      description  `.method` continuation lines
      source doc/rules/c.4.1.md
      variant 1
        description  Blank line required before continuation
      variant 2
        description  No blank line at the same indent
    error 2 OperatorContinuation
      description  Symbolic infix operator continuation
      source doc/rules/c.4.2.md
      variant 1
        description  a multi-line infix operator must terminate the first line, not begin the continuation line
      variant 2
        description  a multi-line infix continuation must be indented <op> columns (found <op>)
      variant 3
        description  a trailing infix operator must be preceded by exactly one space, balancing the line break that follows it
    error 3 HardSpace
      description  Continuation indents after `=>` and heavy `:`
      source doc/rules/c.4.3.md

  subdivision 5 balance
    description  Balance: symmetry of spacing around a token
    error 1 OperatorSpacing
      description  Operator spacing
      source doc/rules/c.5.1.md
    error 2 AssignmentSpacing
      description  Assignment spacing
      source doc/rules/c.5.2.md
    error 3 SymbolicMethodNames
      description  Single space between specific tokens
      source doc/rules/c.5.3.md
    error 4 FormalBlockSpacing
      description  Multi-line block bracket spacing
      source doc/rules/c.5.4.md
    error 5 CompactBracketSpacing
      description  Bracket inner spacing
      source doc/rules/c.5.5.md

  subdivision 6 proximity
    description  Proximity: blank lines and gaps as grouping
    error 1 CommaSpacing
      description  Spacing around commas
      source doc/rules/c.6.1.md
      variant 1
        description  No space before a comma
      variant 2
        description  Exactly one space after a comma
    error 2 ChunkSeparation
      description  Blank-line spacing between sibling declarations
      source doc/rules/c.6.2.md
    error 3 BlankLineRun
      description  Too many consecutive blank lines
      source doc/rules/c.6.3.md
    error 4 ReturnTypeBlank
      description  Blank line after heavy-signature return type
      source doc/rules/c.6.4.md
    error 5 ImportSeparation
      description  Blank line after imports
      source doc/rules/c.6.5.md
    error 6 AnnotationAdjacency
      description  Annotations and following declarations
      source doc/rules/c.6.6.md
      variant 1
        description  Annotation not followed by a declaration
      variant 2
        description  No blank line between annotation and declaration

  subdivision 7 tabulation
    description  Tabulation: vertical alignment across a run of lines
    error 1 CaseAlignment
      description  `=>` alignment in case run
      source doc/rules/c.7.1.md
      variant 1
        description  => of a multi-line case pattern must trail the last pattern token on the same line, not stand alone on its own line
      variant 2
        description  body of a multi-line case pattern must start on the line after =>
      variant 3
        description  exactly one space is required before => in a multi-line case
    error 2 UsingAlignment
      description  `using`-clause alignment
      source doc/rules/c.7.2.md
    error 3 ForComprehensionAlignment
      description  `for`-comprehension layout
      source doc/rules/c.7.3.md
      variant 1
        description  <-/= should be vertically aligned at column <anchorOpCol> (found <gl>)
      variant 2
        description  generator should align with the first generator's LHS at column <anchorLhsCol> (found <gl>)
      variant 3
        description  if filter should align with <-/= at column <anchorOpCol> (found <gl>)
      variant 4
        description  if filter must not be separated from the preceding enumerator by a blank line

  subdivision 8 locatability
    description  Locatability: finding a definition from its name
    error 1 ImportOrdering
      description  Top-level import rules
      source doc/rules/c.8.1.md
      variant 1
        description  No aliases
      variant 2
        description  Group order
      variant 3
        description  Group separation
    error 2 FileNaming
      description  File naming conventions
      source doc/rules/c.8.2.md
    error 3 CompanionOrdering
      description  `object` must precede `class`/`trait`/`enum` of same name
      source doc/rules/c.8.3.md
    error 4 UmbrellaExportCompleteness
      description  Definition not exported to the umbrella package
      source doc/rules/c.8.4.md
    error 5 ExtensionExportCompleteness
      description  Extension method not exported to the umbrella package
      source doc/rules/c.8.5.md

  subdivision 9 soundness
    description  Soundness: what the code claims about itself
    error 1 UnsafeNaming
      description  Unsafe naming
      source doc/rules/c.9.1.md
      variant 1
        description  <name> is gated by <token>, so its name must begin <prefix>
      variant 2
        description  <name> is named as <prefix>, so it must take (using erased <token>)
